<title>USA: White House has not received AMR report yet.</title>
<headline>White House has not received AMR report yet.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House said on Monday it has not yet received a report from the Presidential Emergency Board studying the labor dispute between AMR Corp's American Airlines unit and its pilots union.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not gotten the report yet,&quot; said White House spokeswoman Mary Ellen Glynn. Asked when the administration expected to receive the report, she replied: &quot;possibly today.&quot;</p>
<p>On February 15 President Bill Clinton intervened to stop a strike by American's pilots, naming the Presidential Emergency Board to work with the parties and to make non-binding recommendations within 30 days.</p>
</text>
